  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason (skewness) is not considered by the individual. The individual focuses exclusively on the prize amount and the similarity in winning probabilities, without analyzing how the probabilities are distributed across outcomes. The decision reason requires evaluating the distribution of probability mass — specifically, whether a greater portion is assigned to favorable outcomes — which is absent from the verbal report. The individual’s justification is based on a different criterion (higher prize), not on skewness. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process.",
